    "javaABI": "getLoginInfoMap(): java.util.Map<String,String>, mutable detached result; source loginUi/loginUrl retain nullable Java String properties.",
    "steps": [
      "Read stored raw credential first. A present non-JSON/empty raw value returns an empty Java Map and never derives defaults. A valid stored Map wins even for a version2 marker.",
      "If missing: a LoginUiV2 version2 marker or blank form returns empty, without storing fabricated data.",
      "Static forms parse the retained original RowUi with the same GSON adapters. Filter only type==button; associate name -> default or empty; duplicate names use the last value; retain empty names/other row types according to the original model.",
      "Dynamic <js>/@js forms prepend getLoginJs() and eval in the same original source/Rhino/context. Bind a Java MutableMap result, null book/chapter, and existing source/java/sourceApi/baseUrl. Normalize through the retained existing JsResult seam.",
      "The original source-keyed ThreadLocal recursion guard returns an empty Map on same-thread reentry and always cleans up after success, exception or cancellation.",
      "Only nonempty defaults call the already connected putLoginInfo. A known false put still returns the current defaults Map, exactly as the locked original method; no synthetic success for durable persistence is claimed."
    ],
